r 16th) ","url":"https://www.meetup.com/soulcity/events/316602064/","description":"Good day everyone,\n\nPlease join us for a fun, interactive and enjoyable evening at this wonderful, cozy Firkin Pub location to play some absolute classics like ***pictionary, scattegories, monopoly, clue, cards against humanity, taboo, jenga, hedbanz, euchre, scrabble, balderash, tapple, chess, checker, battleship and always some great new games too!***\n\n\\*Bring along your own games too if you like!\n\n\\*Joined by my other social groups too; so we can anticipate a fabulous turn out with lots of friendly peers to begin our weekend with!\n\n\\*Please note we are at **The Pheasant: A Firkin Pub** at 1999 Avenue Road (roughly 6 blocks north of Lawrence - south of the 401 **(we are in the back dining area to find us)**\n\n*\\*You can also ask the wait staff or bartender if you like to show you to the group (simply ask for Steve's games event)*\n\n**-Free Parking found on residential side streets**\n\n(Event Details Below)\n\nSincerely,\n\nSteve Flemming\n(Organizer/Host )\n\nEvent Details:\n**The Friday Night Mix, Mingle and Games!**\n\n-A chance to play some interactive games we love like ***pictionary, scattergories, taboo, cards against humanity, jenga, monopoly, clue, euchre, scrabble, balderash, tapples, card games,and so many other choices as well!***\n\n\\*Feel free to bring your own games and friends too if you like\n-You'll find it's a cozy, relaxed and enjoyable environment!\n\n***\n\n**Event Fee:** 10 dollars (Cash only at the door) (HST included)\nor by e transfer: **steveflemming11@gmail.com**\n\n***\n\n**Friendly Reminders:**\n\n-Arrive any time after 7:00 pm (in the back area- great for board games, card games and mingling) (event goes to roughly 11:00 pm)\n\n\\*Great dinner menu and food specials provided:\n(One beverage or appetizer minimum upon arrival to support venue)\n\n**Parking and Transportation:**\n\\*Lots of street parking on avenue and free residential parking\nhttps://www.firkinpubs.com/thepheasantandfirkin/\n\n(15-20 minute walk from Yonge & Lawrence subway station-or simply take bus or uber from the station)","startDate":"2026-10-16T23:00:00.000Z","endDate":"","eventStatus":"https://schema.org/EventScheduled","image":"/images/fallbacks/redesign/group-cover-1-square.webp","eventAttendanceMode":"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode","location":{"@type":"Place","name":"The Pheasant: A Firkin Pub","address":{"@type":"PostalAddress","addressLocality":"North York","addressRegion":"ON","addressCountry":"ca","streetAddress":"1999 Avenue Rd, North York, ON"}},"organizer":{"@type":"Organization","name":"Soul City Social Club (Toronto, Canada)","url":"https://www.meetup.com/soulcity/"},"performer":"Soul City Social Club (Toronto, Canada)"},{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"Event","name":"🐾 Give Back: TNR Cat Rescue Volunteer Day","url":"https://www.meetup.com/gta-vibe-and-wander-com/events/316773228/","description":"Please read the details before RSVPing.\n\n🐾 Time to give back, guys\n\nWe’ve partnered with a non-profit animal rescue group to support a TNR (Trap-Neuter-Return) campaign in Scarborough, near 75 Birchmount Ave.\n\nWe’re looking for volunteers to help with\n\n1. 🪤 Setting up traps at designated locations\n2. 🚗 Transporting cats to/from the clinic\n3. 🐱 Feeding cats at designated locations\n\nSome activities require access to your own vehicle, while others simply require your time and willingness to help.\n\nEvery little bit helps, and the cats definitely need us. ❤️?\n\nAnyone allergic to cats, furs or anything related to animals, please do not signup\n\nYou participate this in this event at your own risk. Organizers of this meetup or anyone who is part of this campaign isn't responsible for any untoward incident during your participation in this event .","startDate":"2026-10-16T21:30:00.000Z","endDate":"","eventStatus":"https://schema.org/EventScheduled","image":"/images/fallbacks/redesign/group-cover-1-square.webp","eventAttendanceMode":"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode","location":{"@type":"Place","name":"Scarborough Gardens Arena","address":{"@type":"PostalAddress","addressLocality":"Scarborough","addressRegion":"ON","addressCountry":"ca","streetAddress":"75 Birchmount Road, Scarborough, ON"}},"organizer":{"@type":"Organization","name":"Vibe & Wander","url":"https://www.meetup.com/gta-vibe-and-wander-com/"},"performer":"Vibe & Wander"},{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"Event","name":"Seaton Trail","url":"https://www.meetup.com/toronto-bonfires-meetup-group/events/316622838/","description":"**I’m organizing a fall hike at Seaton Trail in Pickering October 16, at 5 30 p.m.**\n\n**We’ll aim for an 8–10 km hike, taking approximately 3–4 hours at a moderate pace, with breaks to enjoy the fall colours and take pictures.**\n\n**It should be a lovely opportunity to enjoy nature, get some exercise and meet new people.**\n\n**Bring comfortable hiking shoes, water and snacks. Let me know if you’d like to join!**","startDate":"2026-10-16T21:30:00.000Z","endDate":"","eventStatus":"https://schema.org/EventScheduled","image":"/images/fallbacks/redesign/group-cover-1-square.webp","eventAttendanceMode":"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode","location":{"@type":"Place","name":"Whitevale Community Centre","address":{"@type":"PostalAddress","addressLocality":"Pickering","addressRegion":"ON","addressCountry":"ca","streetAddress":"405 Whitevale Rd, Pickering, ON"}},"organizer":{"@type":"Organization","name":"Move With Intention","url":"https://www.meetup.com/toronto-bonfires-meetup-group/"},"performer":"Move With Intention"},{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"Event","name":"Mississauga- let’s speak French/ Parlons français","url":"https://www.meetup.com/diskuto/events/314154994/","description":"Let’s get together to speak French! We’ll enjoy tea/coffee and some icebreaker games. Everyone is welcome.\n\nVenez parler français!\n\nÀ bientôt,\n\nHassane.\n\n\\*Merci beaucoup de vous être inscrit(e) à notre prochaine rencontre! Nous sommes ravis de votre présence.\nAfin de permettre à d’autres de se joindre à nous, nous vous demandons respectueusement :\n\n1. **Si vos plans changent,** veuillez mettre à jour votre statut (passer à 'Non') le plus rapidement possible pour libérer votre place.\n2. **Si vous êtes sur la liste d'attente,** merci de ne pas vous présenter à l'événement. Votre statut doit être confirmé pour pouvoir participer. Veuillez vous inscrire directement aux prochaines dates disponibles.\n\nAu plaisir de vous accueillir!\n\n\\*To allow others to join us, we respectfully ask that you:\n\n* **If your plans change,** please update your RSVP status (change it to 'No') as quickly as possible to free up your spot.\n* **If you are on the waiting list,** please do not show up for the event. Your status must be confirmed to participate. Instead, please register directly for the next available dates.\n\nIMPORTANT:\nVeuillez noter que pour profiter pleinement de nos échanges, une aptitude de base à la conversation est vivement souhaitée : ce groupe est un cercle de discussion convivial et non un cours de langue.\n\nPlease note that to fully enjoy the experience, a basic speaking aptitude is recommended: this group is a social conversation circle, not a formal teaching class.\n\nWe look forward to welcoming you!\n\nPlease join our WhatsApp group:\n\nhttps://chat.whatsapp.com/LRUdXbjpG8I9aph4dU6Go8","startDate":"2026-10-16T22:00:00.000Z","endDate":"","eventStatus":"https://schema.org/EventScheduled","image":"/images/fallbacks/redesign/group-cover-5-square.webp","eventAttendanceMode":"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode","location":{"@type":"Place","name":"Chocolate and love cafe","address":{"@type":"PostalAddress","addressLocality":"Mississauga","addressRegion":"ON","addressCountry":"CA","streetAddress":"5985 Rodeo Dr Unit 14, Mississauga, ON L5R 3V6,, Mississauga, ON"}},"organizer":{"@type":"Organization","name":"Diskuto - Talk with Language Lovers","url":"https://www.meetup.com/diskuto/"},"performer":"Diskuto - Talk with Language Lovers"},{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"Event","name":"20th Anniversary of Cask Days","url":"https://www.meetup.com/beer-171/events/316173138/","description":"## 20 Years of Cask Days\n\nCalling all members - from the O.G. to the newest one - come join us for some fine beer.\n\n**Cask Days** is a celebration of cask-conditioned beer, naturally carbonated, unfiltered and served straight from the cask. Once tapped, it has only a few days to be enjoyed in its prime. We call them Cask Days.\nJoin us October 16–18, 2026, at [282 Campbell Ave](https://maps.app.goo.gl/Bt3PLEYsF8TtVi2J7)., the future home of [Bottega Volo’s](http://bottegavolo.com/) second location. The 20th edition will feature 100+ casks from breweries across Canada, natural wine, great food and music. It all began on the patio of [Bar Volo](http://barvolo.com/) in 2005.\n\nYour Co-Organizers have purchased tickets for Session 2 Friday October 16, 2026 from 5 - 9 p.m. - I have included the ticket information below. They have posted that they are already over 50% sold and they only went on sale August 11, 2026.\n\nPlease visit their website for more information if needed: [https://caskdays.com/cask-days#tickets](https://caskdays.com/cask-days#tickets)\n\nFriday, October 16, 2026\n\n***Session 2: **5:00 pm - 9:00 pm\n\nOne 4-hour session\n4 food and drink tokens\nOfficial Cask Days 2026 mug\n100+ cask-conditioned ales\n19+ with government-issued ID\nLimited to 500 guests\n[282 Campbell Ave.](https://maps.app.goo.gl/Bvxpgwy3B2dAcnKcA) (Clock Factory Building)\n$50\n- tax & processing fees\n\nLink to buy tickets: [https://cask-days.bloomtickets.ca/event/2120?20thAnnualCaskDaysBeerFestival](https://cask-days.bloomtickets.ca/event/2120?20thAnnualCaskDaysBeerFestival)\n\nIf you can't go to Session 2 please try and attend one of the other sessions as it really is an experience.\n\nHOW IT WORKS\n\n## CASK AVAILABILITY\n\nCask ale waits for no one. Once tapped, each cask has only a few glorious days at its best—and when it’s gone, it’s gone. We’ll have just one cask of each beer, so if something special has caught your eye, book an earlier session and get to it before the crowd does.\n\n## SERVINGS & GLASSWARE\n\nCask Days is a tasting journey, so every beer is poured in a 5 oz serving. Most pours cost one token, while specialty and stronger ales cost two. Your official Cask Days 2026 mug is included with your ticket and is yours to keep and reuse throughout the festival.\n\n## FOOD & DRINK TOKENS\n\nTokens are your festival currency, good for cask ales and food at every session. Each token is worth $3.75 plus tax, and Session 1–4 tickets include 4x tokens to get you started. Need more? Tokens will be available for purchase at the event. Tokens are non-refundable.\n\nLINEUP\nFeaturing cask-ales from…\n\n#### ONTARIO All My Friends • Amsterdam • AURUM• Badlands • Bellwoods • Beyond the Pale • Bickford • Black Lab • Blood Brothers • Bobcaygeon • Burdock • C’est What Durham • Clifford • Common Good • Conjure • Dominion City • Fairweather • Ferm Farm • Fine Balance • Godspeed • Granite • Great Lakes • Indie Alehouse • Left Field • Lovebird • Matron • McGrath • Muddy York • Nickel Brook • Paradise Grapevine • Rainhard • Revel Cider • Rorschach • Rouge River • Short Finger • Silversmith • Slake • Something in the Water • Steadfast • Third Moon • Tooth and Nail • Town • TRUE HISTORY• Two Loons • Volo • Wellington • Willibald\n\n#### QUEBEC • 5e Baron • Albion • Dieu du Ciel! • Dunham • Hopfenstark • Isle de Garde • Mellön • Messorem • WILLS • NOVA SCOTIA • Big Spruce • Boxing Rock • North • Propeller • Schoolhouse • Stillwell • Tatamagouche • ALBERTA • Ale Architect • Annex Ale Project • Bent Stick • Blind Enthusiasm • Blindman • Cabin • Dandy • The Establishment • BRITISH COLUMBIA • Four Winds • Luppolo • Slow Hand • Small Gods • Superflux • Temporal Artisan Ales\n\n[CASK LIST COMING SOON!](https://caskdays.com/cask-days)\n\n## WHAT IS CASK ALE?\n\nBefore metal kegs, CO₂, and refrigeration, beer was served as cask-conditioned ale. Unlike most beer, cask ale continues fermenting in the cask until just before it's poured, creating its naturally gentle carbonation. Before serving, the cask is vented to release excess gas and the yeast settles to the bottom. The result is a beer that's lightly carbonated, served at cellar temperature, and exceptionally fresh, with vibrant flavour and character. Once tapped, a cask is best enjoyed within just a few days.** We call those days, Cask Days.**\n\nTheir website has a lot of FAQ's.\n\nHope to see a lot of members there.","startDate":"2026-10-16T21:00:00.000Z","endDate":"","eventStatus":"https://schema.org/EventScheduled","image":"/images/fallbacks/redesign/group-cover-4-square.webp","eventAttendanceMode":"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode","location":{"@type":"Place","name":"Cask Days Beer Festival","address":{"@type":"PostalAddress","addressLocality":"Toronto","addressRegion":"ON","addressCountry":"ca","streetAddress":"282 Campbell Ave. (Clock Factory Building), Toronto, ON"}},"organizer":{"@type":"Organization","name":"Toronto Beer Lovers","url":"https://www.meetup.com/beer-171/"},"performer":"Toronto Beer Lovers"},{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"Event","name":"🎬Movie: Whalefall -  Food & Drinks after the movie 🍿!","url":"https://www.meetup.com/toronto-movies-and-social-group/events/316155632/","description":"🎬 Let’s Go to the Movies (and Actually Talk… or Not)\n\nWhether you're a film nerd, popcorn enthusiast, or just looking for a chill night out with interesting people — this one's for you.\n\nWe’re heading out to see a movie together, then grabbing food or drinks after. If the film's great (or terrible), we’ll probably talk about it forever. If it’s just okay, we’ll talk about it for 10 minutes and move on to everything else — books, dating apps, weird dreams, how Toronto keeps getting more expensive, etc.\n\nThe vibe is relaxed, friendly, and not too serious. No film degree needed. No icebreakers. No pressure to “perform.” Just come enjoy the film, connect with some thoughtful people, and see where the night goes Click here to watch trailer!\n\n🎞️ **Movie Title + Trailer:** [\\[Click here to watch trailer!\\]](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=67ho3OxCmmM)\n\n📖 **📖 Plot Summary:** Centering on a scuba diver in search of his deceased father’s remains who gets swallowed by an 80-foot, 60-ton sperm whale and has only one hour to escape before his oxygen runs out. After giving up on life, the young man is surprised to find a reason to live in the most dangerous and unlikely of places.\n\n***\n\n### 🗓️ **Event Details**\n\n📍 **Meetup Time:** 6:00 PM (Final time + theatre announced Tuesday of event week)\n🎬 **Movie Start Time:** TBA\n⏱️ **Runtime:** TBA\n📌 **Meetup Spot:** To be confirmed (based on theatre)\n🎟️ **Cost:**\n\n* **$11.50** for *CineClub* members\n* **$16.00** regular admission\n👉 You are responsible for buying your own ticket.\n\n**🪑 Reserved Seating:**\nYou must buy your ticket *before* signing up. You'll be asked where you're sitting so we can all sit together! However, members are welcome to sit anywhere that works for them.\n🎫 Buy your ticket here: [https://www.cineplex.com](https://www.cineplex.com)\n📍🪑 **Where I will be sitting:**\n\n🍿 **After the Movie:**\nYes, we’re heading out after! It’s not just a movie night — it’s a social night. Let's talk, laugh, and dissect every plot twist.\n\n***\n\n### ✅ **Before You Sign Up**\n\n* Please **buy your ticket first** — seating is limited!\n* When signing up, let us know your **seat number** so we can try to group everyone together.\n* You can still sign up or just **show up on the day** if you’re not sure you can make it — we’re flexible!\n\n📲 **Join Our WhatsApp Group:**[ Click here to join](https://chat.whatsapp.com/H59mSCbsAi018gYANrKAnc)\n🎟️ **Join Cineplex’s CineClub for discounts**: [https://www.cineplex.com/cineclub](https://www.cineplex.com/cineclub)\n🎁 **Get your SCENE Card** for free movies and points: [https://www.scene.ca](https://www.scene.ca)\n\n***\n\n### 🎥 **A Quick Word About Movie Etiquette**\n\nWe love a great film experience. Please:\n\n* Turn off your phone\n* Don’t talk during the movie\n* Be respectful of others\n\nRepeat offenders will be removed from the group — we take our cinema seriously (but with snacks).\n\n***\n\n### 👥 **About the Group**\n\nThis event is open to everyone — single, not single, shy, social, new in town or a long-time local. We're a group for people who love movies *and* making real connections. We also do walks, hikes, restaurants, arts & culture — come be part of it!\n🎬 **Organized by:** Mathew\n📧 Questions? Reach out: **torontomoviesandoutings@hotmail.com**","startDate":"2026-10-16T22:00:00.000Z","endDate":"","eventStatus":"https://schema.org/EventScheduled","image":"/images/fallbacks/redesign/group-cover-1-square.webp","eventAttendanceMode":"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode","location":{"@type":"Place","address":{"@type":"PostalAddress","addressLocality":"","addressRegion":"","addressCountry":""}},"organizer":{"@type":"Organization","name":"Toronto Movies & Social Group - Celebrating 14 Years!","url":"https://www.meetup.com/toronto-movies-and-social-group/"},"performer":"Toronto Movies & Social Group - Celebrating 14 Years!"},{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"Event","name":"Darkestest Secrets! There Will be Blood - Hosted by HH Holmes (RETURN FOR 2026)","url":"https://www.meetup.com/the-history-of-parkdale/events/315426659/","description":"\\*\\***The Toronto History Walks Yearly Pass is available. Get it now for $125.00 for 1 year of unlimited tours, email**\n**torontohistorywalks@gmail.com**\n**for more information or for signing up!\\*\\***\n\n\\*\\* **Please note: Please e-transfer the ticket amount when booking your space for this tour! You can e-transfer to the following email at:**\n**torontohistorywalks@gmail.com**\n\nStart the fall season on a high note with this frightening walking tour hosted by **HH Holmes** the most prolific serial killer in American History. Considered the first serial killer he will conduct this entire tour from beginning to end. It will keep you up late at night for days.\n\nThis tour will be hosted and conducted by a man who committed some of the most vicious crimes, and there is a Toronto connection to it all. He loved Toronto and wished it well.\n\nFrom serial killers to strange disappearances, this tour will explore some of the most disturbing true life cases, solved and unsolved, over the last 140 years here in Toronto. From old Sayer Street in the old Ward to Hospital Row. In areas that one would find quiet, and comfortable, there are demons hiding, some in plain sight. Like HH Holmes said just before he dropped through the trap door of the gallows at Moyamensing Prison; \"I always had the Devil in me.\"\n\nThis is not a **ghost** tour but a continuation of the Dark History of Toronto Series that started back in 2019 with Volume 1.\n\nThis horrific walking tour is for all levels and walkers. **But this tour is not for children under the age of 12**\n\nThe tour begins at the **Toronto Sign** in Nathan Philips Square. The tour ends at Bay and College Streets.\n\n**Please book early if you wish to attend this event in October! And Mr. Holmes will be waiting, patiently for your prompt RSVP!**\n\nThis tour has a ticket price of $15.00 person!\n\n\\*\\* **Please note: Please e-transfer the ticket amount when booking your space for this tour! You can e-transfer to the following email at:**\n**torontohistorywalks@gmail.com**","startDate":"2026-10-16T23:00:00.000Z","endDate":"","eventStatus":"https://schema.org/EventScheduled","image":"/images/fallbacks/redesign/group-cover-2-square.webp","eventAttendanceMode":"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode","location":{"@type":"Place","name":"Nathan Philips Square","address":{"@type":"PostalAddress","addressLocality":"Toronto","addressRegion":"ON","addressCountry":"ca","streetAddress":"100 Queen St W, Toronto, ON"}},"organizer":{"@type":"Organization","name":"Toronto History Walks","url":"https://www.meetup.com/the-history-of-parkdale/"},"performer":"Toronto History Walks"},{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"Event","name":"Casual Board Games and Pub Social After","url":"https://www.meetup.com/boardgamestoronto/events/316441934/","description":"The Board Games event is a fun, sociable and charitable event\n\nWe are a fun, friendly and kind group of people mostly in our 20s, 30s and 40s. Beginners are welcome! We are a very inclusive and social group and we teach people how to play games they have not played before :)\n\nWe provide a variety of 40+ board games. The games usually take 5 or 10 minutes to learn and 30 to 60 minutes to play.\n\nPlay in French: On the last Friday of the month, we're offering a table where the games are played in French. Anyone with an intermediate level of French who wants to practice while playing is welcome to join. Just ask for Philippe when you arrive.\n\n**Time**\n\n*Board Games Start time: 630pm\n- Board Games end time: 10pm\n*Eat / Drink/ Socialise at a nearby pub afterwards\n\n**Location**\n\n30 Leeds St, Toronto, ON M6G 3R8 (Ukrainian Catholic Church of the Holy Protection)\n\nThe entrance to the board game room is at the back of the Church. There is a sign on the door that says BOARD GAMES GROUP.\n\nPlease use the map provided on the event page also.\n\nPayment\n**There are two ways to pay**\n**10 by Cash - coins are not accepted. Only bills.****\n**11.55 by Debit/Credit card\n\n**Charity Donations**\n\n- This is a not-for-profit initiative. Revenue go towards covering costs of the event including venue, insurance marketing, refreshments and board games. Any surplus revenue is donated to charity\n\n**Food and drink**\n\n*Everyone will get cookies/candy for free\n- Cups will be provided for tap water\n*Bring your own food and drink.\n- Please do not bring CHIPS AND CRACKERS as they make a mess and are greasy\n***ALCOHOL IS PROHIBITED AND WE HAVE A ZERO TOLERANCE POLICY ON THIS - there are no second chances**\n\nPhotos will be taken at the event and posted publicly for marketing purposes. Please only attend if you are ok with this or tell me when you arrive that you do not want to be in any photos\n\nThe event is officially hosted by Ace of Math Learning Program Ontario Inc.","startDate":"2026-10-16T22:30:00.000Z","endDate":"","eventStatus":"https://schema.org/EventScheduled","image":"/images/fallbacks/redesign/group-cover-4-square.webp","eventAttendanceMode":"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode","location":{"@type":"Place","name":"Ukrainian Catholic Church of the Holy Protection","address":{"@type":"PostalAddress","addressLocality":"Toronto","addressRegion":"ON","addressCountry":"ca","streetAddress":"30 Leeds St, Toronto, ON M6G 3R8, Toronto, ON"}},"organizer":{"@type":"Organization","name":"Board Games and Social","url":"https://www.meetup.com/boardgamestoronto/"},"performer":"Board Games and Social"},{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"Event","name":"Tantric Family Constellation: Temple of Love & Money","url":"https://www.meetup.com/toronto-tantra-circle/events/316728491/","description":"**TANTRIC FAMILY CONSTELLATIONS**\n**Tantric Temple Mysteries**\n\n**This is the project overview only.**\n**Themes and dates may change.**\n\n**To find the exact topic, date and register, please join:**\n\n**t.me/TorontoTantra**\n**t.me/AndyTherapist**\n\n**⸻**\n\n**About this event**\n\n**Tantric Family Constellations is a group practice combining Archetypal / Family Constellations with a living tantric Temple space.**\n\n**Each meeting has its own theme.**\n\n**For example:**\n\n**Love & Money • Ancient Languages of Love • Love & Loneliness • Masculine & Feminine • Desire & Freedom • Relationship Patterns**\n\n**The theme gives us a field to explore — but every participant discovers their own personal story inside it.**\n\n**⸻**\n\n**Part 1 — Discover your pattern**\n\n**We begin by exploring different dimensions of the evening’s theme together.**\n\n**Then each participant goes through a mini-constellation to see their own pattern, model or hidden dynamic.**\n\n**Instead of only thinking about the question, you can see how its different forces are arranged for you:**\n\n**What attracts you?**\n**What do you avoid?**\n**Where does your energy stop?**\n**What are you moving toward?**\n\n**This creates a personal map for the second part of the evening.**\n\n**⸻**\n\n**Part 2 — Enter the Temple**\n\n**Then we open the Tantric Temple.**\n\n**The constellation points become living centers in the space.**\n\n**Participants are free to move between them, following their own inner process.**\n\n**You may stay with one energy, move toward another, step away, return, observe what happens in your body, or allow yourself to gradually absorb a quality that previously felt distant.**\n\n**At the same time, you encounter other participants moving through their own paths.**\n\n**Through presence, movement and consensual interaction, the personal constellation becomes a living group field.**\n\n**There is no fixed choreography and no need to perform.**\n\n**You follow your own rhythm.**\n\n**The practice is about allowing yourself to experience, embody and integrate the different energies of the constellation rather than only understand them intellectually.**\n\n**⸻**\n\n**Why “Temple”?**\n\n**The Temple is a temporary tantric space where symbolic and archetypal energies can be experienced through the body, movement and connection with others.**\n\n**The journey is individual, but it happens inside a shared field.**\n\n**You may discover that a quality which looked abstract during the constellation becomes much more understandable once you can actually move toward it, stay with it and experience it in contact with others.**\n\n**⸻**\n\n**No previous constellation or tantra experience is required.**\n\n**Participation is voluntary, and you can always choose your own level of involvement and contact.**\n\n**The space is based on:**\n\n**consent • respect • confidentiality • personal boundaries • freedom of movement**\n\n**This is a transpersonal personal-growth practice.**\n\n**Details, themes, dates and registration:**\n**t.me/TorontoTantra**\n\n**TICKETS**\n\n1. **Regular Ticket — $100 CAD**\n1. **Early Bird Ticket — $65 CAD**\n**If you register and pay before August 31.**\n**3. Supportive Ticket — $55 CAD**\n**For people with limited financial resources.**\n**4. Bring a Friend — $150 CAD for 2 people**\n\n**If the price is too much for you, send a personal message on Telegram: t.me/AndyTherapist to ask about volunteer options.**\n\n**HOW TO PAY**\n\n**Send an Interac e-Transfer to:**\n**andy.litvinov@gmail.com**\n**After payment, send a screenshot of the confirmation to: t.me/AndyTherapist**\n**Please mention which event you are registering for.**\n\n**After registration, you will be added to the participants’ group.**\n\n**If you have any questions, feel free to message:**\n**t.me/AndyTherapist**\n**Toronto Tantra community:**\n**t.me/TorontoTantra**","startDate":"2026-10-16T23:00:00.000Z","endDate":"","eventStatus":"https://schema.org/EventScheduled","image":"/images/fallbacks/redesign/group-cover-2-square.webp","eventAttendanceMode":"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode","location":{"@type":"Place","address":{"@type":"PostalAddress","addressLocality":"","addressRegion":"","addressCountry":""}},"organizer":{"@type":"Organization","name":"T.me/TorontoTantra Circle","url":"https://www.meetup.com/toronto-tantra-circle/"},"performer":"T.me/TorontoTantra Circle"},{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"Event","name":"Cuddle Club - platonic body nourishing.","url":"https://www.meetup.com/toronto-tantra-circle/events/316727876/","description":"**CUDDLE CLUB.**\n**Have you tried that?**\n\n**In Amsterdam cuddle events are sold out quickly. Even few different Cuddle clubs are happening at the same day. It's so popular there.**\n\n**In Toronto there** **is** **nearly no Cuddle clubs yet.**\n**But we are doing that.**\n**Join our tantric group and leave a message in comments if you wanna join the waiting list.**\n**T.me/TorontoTantra**\n**___**\n**About this event**\n**• What is the cuddle club?**\n\n**It’s a cozy evening to experience how deeply nourishing it can feel to be held, without any romantic or sexual expectations. A space where people can come together to share love and touch. We cuddle platonically, the way you’d hold a child or a kitten.**\n\n**• What will we be doing?**\n\n**Facilitator will guide you through some gentle exercises to help you unwind after your day, soften into your body, and calm your nervous system. We aim to make you feel safe in your own body, which can help you connect with others.**\n\n**• Cuddle puddle perfection**\n\n**Everything is by invitation, but we will guide you into a beautifully structured cuddle puddle. It is a very comfortable, welcoming way of cuddling where you are held and touched by multiple people at the same time. Chances are you’ll float home afterwards, high on oxytocin.**\n\n**• Important terms & agreements:**\n1. **Keep it platonic: we cuddle without romantic or sexual expectations or escalations**\n1. **Take care of yourself and others: communicate and respect boundaries**\n1. **Be here fully: This is a sober space. No drugs, no alcohol. No phones.**\n\n**Details in telegram group:**\n**t.me/TorontoTantra**\n\n**TICKETS**\n**Regular Ticket — $50 CAD**\n**Early Bird Ticket — $35 CAD (If you register and pay before August 31).**\n**Supportive Ticket — $25 CAD (For students and people with low financial income).**\n**Combo — $60 CAD for 2 people (Bring a friend).**\n\n**Free participation.**\n**We want everyone to have an opportunity to participate. If the price is too much for you, send a personal message on Telegram: t.me/AndyTherapist to ask about volunteer options.**\n\n**If you have any questions, feel free to message:**\n**t.me/AndyTherapist**\n**t.me/TorontoTantra**","startDate":"2026-10-16T22:00:00.000Z","endDate":"","eventStatus":"https://schema.org/EventScheduled","image":"/images/fallbacks/redesign/group-cover-2-square.webp","eventAttendanceMode":"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode","location":{"@type":"Place","address":{"@type":"PostalAddress","addressLocality":"","addressRegion":"","addressCountry":""}},"organizer":{"@type":"Organization","name":"T.me/TorontoTantra Circle","url":"https://www.meetup.com/toronto-tantra-circle/"},"performer":"T.me/TorontoTantra Circle"},{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"Event","name":"MASSAGE CLUB & BODY PSYCHOTHERAPY","url":"https://www.meetup.com/toronto-tantra-circle/events/316727509/","description":"MASSAGE CLUB & BODY PSYCHOTHERAPY\nThis is the project overview only!\nDates might change.\n\nTo find the exact dates and register for the event, please join our Telegram group:\n\nT.me/TorontoTantra\nT.me/AndyTherapist\n\nMASSAGE & BODY PSYCHOTHERAPY CLUB\n\nHave you ever explored massage not only as relaxation, but also as a way to reconnect with your body, emotions, and nervous system?\n\nIn Toronto there are many massage services, but not many spaces where people can safely learn, practice and exchange conscious touch together.\n\nWe would like to create such a club.\n\nA warm, respectful space for people interested in massage, bodywork, somatic practices and body-oriented psychotherapy.\n\nYou don’t need professional massage experience. Beginners are welcome.\n\nJoin our group and leave a message if you would like to be added to the waiting list.\nt.me/TorontoTantra\n\nAbout this event\n\n• What is the Massage & Body Psychotherapy Club?\n\nIt is a practice evening where we explore conscious touch, relaxation, massage techniques and simple body-oriented therapeutic exercises.\n\nThe purpose is not only to relax muscles, but also to develop better contact with your body, reduce stress and learn how safe touch can support emotional regulation and connection.\n\n• What will we be doing?\n\nDepending on the evening, we may explore:\n\n- simple relaxation massage techniques\n- conscious touch and body awareness\n- grounding and nervous-system regulation\n- breathing and relaxation exercises\n- somatic and body-psychotherapy exercises\n- practicing giving and receiving\n- communication of boundaries and consent\n\nPractices can be done in pairs or small groups and will be guided step by step.\n\n• Massage exchange\n\nOne of the main parts of the club is a structured massage exchange.\n\nYou can experience both sides:\ngiving touch and receiving touch.\n\nThe goal is not to perform a “perfect massage,” but to become more sensitive to another person’s body, learn to listen through your hands, communicate clearly and discover what kind of touch feels supportive.\n\nImportant terms & agreements\n\nConsent first: every exercise and every touch is optional.\n\nRespect boundaries: you can say yes, no, stop, slower, softer or change the practice at any moment.\n\nKeep it therapeutic: this is a bodywork and personal-development space, not a sexual service or dating event.\n\nStay present: no alcohol or recreational drugs during the event.\n\nConfidentiality: personal experiences shared during the practice stay within the group.\n\nThe club may be interesting for people curious about:\n\nmassage • bodywork • somatic therapy • body-oriented psychotherapy • conscious touch • nervous-system regulation • relaxation • tantra-inspired body awareness\n\nDetails, dates and registration:\nt.me/TorontoTantra","startDate":"2026-10-16T21:00:00.000Z","endDate":"","eventStatus":"https://schema.org/EventScheduled","image":"/images/fallbacks/redesign/group-cover-2-square.webp","eventAttendanceMode":"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode","location":{"@type":"Place","address":{"@type":"PostalAddress","addressLocality":"","addressRegion":"","addressCountry":""}},"organizer":{"@type":"Organization","name":"T.me/TorontoTantra Circle","url":"https://www.meetup.com/toronto-tantra-circle/"},"performer":"T.me/TorontoTantra Circle"},{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"Event","name":"Friday VIP Future Nightclub for free for ladies ","url":"https://www.meetup.com/nightlife-society-vip-club-nights/events/316654620/","description":"🎉 Future Nightclub Fridays \\| VIP Night Out 🎉\n📍 Future Nightclub\n🗓 Every Friday\n⏰ 10:30 PM\nJoin us this Friday for a fun VIP night out at Future Nightclub.\n✅ Free entry until 11:30 pm\n\nJust say “Ammar Alomari” at the door for the guestlist.\nFor the guys check on the guest list to get your free drink and a discount for the door cover.\n\n🥂 VIP booth access and free entry before 12 midnight\n\nComing alone? No worries. We usually have 40+ people joining every weekend, including friends, ticket guests, and new people from our meetup group, so you will have people to connect with.\n📌 Find us at the main booth.\n\n🙌 19+ only with valid government-issued ID. Entry is subject to venue rules, capacity, and door policy.\nSee you Friday!","startDate":"2026-10-17T02:30:00.000Z","endDate":"","eventStatus":"https://schema.org/EventScheduled","image":"/images/fallbacks/redesign/group-cover-4-square.webp","eventAttendanceMode":"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode","location":{"@type":"Place","name":"Future","address":{"@type":"PostalAddress","addressLocality":"Toronto","addressRegion":"ON","addressCountry":"ca","streetAddress":"570 Queen St W, Toronto, ON M5V 2B5, Canada, Toronto, ON"}},"organizer":{"@type":"Organization","name":"Nightlife Society | VIP Club Nights","url":"https://www.meetup.com/nightlife-society-vip-club-nights/"},"performer":"Nightlife Society | VIP Club Nights"}]</script><link rel="preload" href="https://secure.mee