hotoInfo:324215289"}},"Member:170566932":{"__typename":"Member","id":"170566932","name":"Meenakshi","memberPhoto":{"__ref":"PhotoInfo:316707318"}},"Member:427556190":{"__typename":"Member","id":"427556190","name":"Nigel Champion","memberPhoto":{"__ref":"PhotoInfo:320712171"}},"Event:316173138":{"__typename":"Event","id":"316173138","title":"20th Anniversary of Cask Days","dateTime":"2026-10-16T17:00:00-04:00","description":"## 20 Years of Cask Days\n\nCalling all members - from the O.G. to the newest one - come join us for some fine beer.\n\n**Cask Days** is a celebration of cask-conditioned beer, naturally carbonated, unfiltered and served straight from the cask. Once tapped, it has only a few days to be enjoyed in its prime. We call them Cask Days.\nJoin us October 16–18, 2026, at [282 Campbell Ave](https://maps.app.goo.gl/Bt3PLEYsF8TtVi2J7)., the future home of [Bottega Volo’s](http://bottegavolo.com/) second location. The 20th edition will feature 100+ casks from breweries across Canada, natural wine, great food and music. It all began on the patio of [Bar Volo](http://barvolo.com/) in 2005.\n\nYour Co-Organizers have purchased tickets for Session 2 Friday October 16, 2026 from 5 - 9 p.m. - I have included the ticket information below. They have posted that they are already over 50% sold and they only went on sale August 11, 2026.\n\nPlease visit their website for more information if needed: [https://caskdays.com/cask-days#tickets](https://caskdays.com/cask-days#tickets)\n\nFriday, October 16, 2026\n\n***Session 2: **5:00 pm - 9:00 pm\n\nOne 4-hour session\n4 food and drink tokens\nOfficial Cask Days 2026 mug\n100+ cask-conditioned ales\n19+ with government-issued ID\nLimited to 500 guests\n[282 Campbell Ave.](https://maps.app.goo.gl/Bvxpgwy3B2dAcnKcA) (Clock Factory Building)\n$50\n- tax \u0026 processing fees\n\nLink to buy tickets: [https://cask-days.bloomtickets.ca/event/2120?20thAnnualCaskDaysBeerFestival](https://cask-days.bloomtickets.ca/event/2120?20thAnnualCaskDaysBeerFestival)\n\nIf you can't go to Session 2 please try and attend one of the other sessions as it really is an experience.\n\nHOW IT WORKS\n\n## CASK AVAILABILITY\n\nCask ale waits for no one. Once tapped, each cask has only a few glorious days at its best—and when it’s gone, it’s gone. We’ll have just one cask of each beer, so if something special has caught your eye, book an earlier session and get to it before the crowd does.\n\n## SERVINGS \u0026 GLASSWARE\n\nCask Days is a tasting journey, so every beer is poured in a 5 oz serving. Most pours cost one token, while specialty and stronger ales cost two. Your official Cask Days 2026 mug is included with your ticket and is yours to keep and reuse throughout the festival.\n\n## FOOD \u0026 DRINK TOKENS\n\nTokens are your festival currency, good for cask ales and food at every session. Each token is worth $3.75 plus tax, and Session 1–4 tickets include 4x tokens to get you started. Need more? Tokens will be available for purchase at the event. Tokens are non-refundable.\n\nLINEUP\nFeaturing cask-ales from…\n\n#### ONTARIO All My Friends • Amsterdam • AURUM• Badlands • Bellwoods • Beyond the Pale • Bickford • Black Lab • Blood Brothers • Bobcaygeon • Burdock • C’est What Durham • Clifford • Common Good • Conjure • Dominion City • Fairweather • Ferm Farm • Fine Balance • Godspeed • Granite • Great Lakes • Indie Alehouse • Left Field • Lovebird • Matron • McGrath • Muddy York • Nickel Brook • Paradise Grapevine • Rainhard • Revel Cider • Rorschach • Rouge River • Short Finger • Silversmith • Slake • Something in the Water • Steadfast • Third Moon • Tooth and Nail • Town • TRUE HISTORY• Two Loons • Volo • Wellington • Willibald\n\n#### QUEBEC • 5e Baron • Albion • Dieu du Ciel! • Dunham • Hopfenstark • Isle de Garde • Mellön • Messorem • WILLS • NOVA SCOTIA • Big Spruce • Boxing Rock • North • Propeller • Schoolhouse • Stillwell • Tatamagouche • ALBERTA • Ale Architect • Annex Ale Project • Bent Stick • Blind Enthusiasm • Blindman • Cabin • Dandy • The Establishment • BRITISH COLUMBIA • Four Winds • Luppolo • Slow Hand • Small Gods • Superflux • Temporal Artisan Ales\n\n[CASK LIST COMING SOON!](https://caskdays.com/cask-days)\n\n## WHAT IS CASK ALE?\n\nBefore metal kegs, CO₂, and refrigeration, beer was served as cask-conditioned ale. Unlike most beer, cask ale continues fermenting in the cask until just before it's poured, creating its naturally gentle carbonation. Before serving, the cask is vented to release excess gas and the yeast settles to the bottom. The result is a beer that's lightly carbonated, served at cellar temperature, and exceptionally fresh, with vibrant flavour and character. Once tapped, a cask is best enjoyed within just a few days.** We call those days, Cask Days.**\n\nTheir website has a lot of FAQ's.\n\nHope to see a lot of members there.","eventType":"PHYSICAL","eventUrl":"https://www.meetup.com/beer-171/events/316173138/","isAttending":false,"isSaved":false,"maxTickets":0,"rsvpState":"JOIN_OPEN","featuredEventPhoto":{"__ref":"PhotoInfo:535730997"},"displayPhoto":{"__ref":"PhotoInfo:535730997"},"feeSettings":null,"group":{"__ref":"Group:602760"},"socialProofInsights":{"__typename":"SocialProofInsights","isTrendingEvent":false,"totalInterestedUsers":35,"interestedUsersSample":[{"__typename":"Member","memberPhoto":{"__ref":"PhotoInfo:325803712"}},{"__typename":"Member","memberPhoto":{"__ref":"PhotoInfo:256725431"}},{"__typename":"Member","memberPhoto":{"__ref":"PhotoInfo:266705953"}},{"__typename":"Member","memberPhoto":{"__ref":"PhotoInfo:255916605"}},{"__typename":"Member","memberPhoto":{"__ref":"PhotoInfo:324215289"}},{"__typename":"Member","memberPhoto":{"__ref":"PhotoInfo:316707318"}},{"__typename":"Member","memberPhoto":{"__ref":"PhotoInfo:320712171"}}]},"rsvps":{"__typename":"RsvpConnection","totalCount":10,"edges":[{"__typename":"RsvpEdge","node":{"__typename":"Rsvp","isHost":true,"member":{"__ref":"Member:85057202"}}},{"__typename":"Rsv